1
00:00:02,870 --> 00:00:07,020
<i>Typhoon No. 2 continues 
to grow and is moving north,</i>

2
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:11,770
<i>causing unstable weather conditions 
in the Kanto and Tohoku regions.</i>

3
00:00:10,990 --> 00:00:21,000
SUBJECT: TYPHOON NO. 2 APPROACHING
YOU ARE ENCOURAGED TO WORK FROM HOME TODAY.

4
00:00:11,770 --> 00:00:18,060
<i>At this time, the typhoon is still generating 
strong winds, but is expected to weaken.</i>

5
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:21,520
<i>There is a possibility that the typhoon 
will approach the Kanto region again</i>

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:30,000
TYPHOON NO. 2

7
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:23,790
<i>between tonight and tomorrow morning.</i>

8
00:00:23,790 --> 00:00:28,190
<i>It's moving quickly, and the wind 
and rain may suddenly strengthen.</i>

9
00:00:28,190 --> 00:00:32,970
<i>Please avoid unnecessary outings, 
and regularly check recent updates.</i>

10
00:00:30,430 --> 00:00:33,320
They're tellin' us to stay home,

11
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:35,880
there are some things I can't 
do unless I'm at the office.

12
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:38,300
I gotta take samples to 
the meeting place, too...

13
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:41,830
Wait. It's one thing for me, 
but what about Kamegawa?

14
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:45,850
As a mentor, am I s'posed to allow 
the newbie to show up to work

15
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:48,090
when a typhoon is comin'?

16
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:51,700
But Kamegawa needs to 
attend the meeting, too...

17
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:55,030
And there's that deadline 
for the sunscreen proposal...

18
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:10,190
This ain't the time for me to daydream!

19
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:17,550
Rainy weather pumps: check!

20
00:01:17,550 --> 00:01:19,970
Towel in bag: check!

21
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:24,640
Today, I'm gonna finish work early 
so I can send Kamegawa home!

22
00:01:42,450 --> 00:01:46,120
MY AWKWARD SENPAI

23
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:15,960
EPISODE 5: IT'S ALL THE TYPHOON'S FAULT

24
00:03:12,470 --> 00:03:14,720
"It's All the Typhoon's Fault!"

25
00:03:18,710 --> 00:03:21,310
Is everyone working remotely?

26
00:03:22,850 --> 00:03:24,580
Then that means...

27
00:03:25,260 --> 00:03:26,670
Good morning.

28
00:03:30,370 --> 00:03:32,190
M-Morning...

29
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:36,640
<i>I'm alone with Kamegawa...</i>

30
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:38,980
The wind's really strong today!

31
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:42,360
Looks like everyone is working from home.

32
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:48,000
Let's finish our work early before the 
typhoon keeps us from getting home.

33
00:03:48,490 --> 00:03:49,640
Yes, ma'am!

34
00:04:10,350 --> 00:04:14,370
<i>Normally, this place is bustlin', 
but today it's just the two of us.</i>

35
00:04:14,370 --> 00:04:16,490
<i>I'm gettin' a li'l nervous.</i>

36
00:04:16,980 --> 00:04:20,460
<i>No, I should be used to 
being with Kamegawa by now!</i>

37
00:04:20,830 --> 00:04:24,800
<i>The two of us even had to share a room 
during the Okinawa business trip...</i>

38
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:29,380
<i>Wait. Now that I think about it,</i>

39
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:31,690
<i>that situation could have been avoided.</i>

40
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:35,510
<i>Gotta focus on my work!</i>

41
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:51,350
It's really raining now.

42
00:04:51,350 --> 00:04:54,350
I was hoping we could leave 
while the weather was okay.

43
00:04:54,350 --> 00:04:55,890
It couldn't be helped.

44
00:04:55,890 --> 00:04:57,880
Are your shoes waterproof?

45
00:04:57,880 --> 00:05:00,860
Oh, these are the ones I always wear.

46
00:05:03,690 --> 00:05:08,570
Could it be that your shoes 
are okay in the rain, Senpai?

47
00:05:08,570 --> 00:05:09,580
Yeah.

48
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:13,100
I didn't know there were cute 
rain boots like those.

49
00:05:14,570 --> 00:05:17,660
What kind of person would wear 
normal shoes during weather like this?

50
00:05:17,660 --> 00:05:21,490
Business-style rain shoes exist, 
so be prepared next time.

51
00:05:21,490 --> 00:05:23,300
Yes, ma'am. I'm sorry.

52
00:05:26,380 --> 00:05:28,500
It's raining cats and dogs.

53
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:32,630
The forecast did say that the 
typhoon was moving quickly.

54
00:05:36,630 --> 00:05:39,000
I forgot my umbrella...

55
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:39,940
What?!

56
00:05:41,110 --> 00:05:43,970
<i>What is this? I gave Kamegawa 
a talkin'-to about shoes,</i>

57
00:05:43,970 --> 00:05:46,950
<i>but I'm the one who forgot an umbrella!</i>

58
00:05:46,950 --> 00:05:50,450
<i>Rain means bring an umbrella! An umbrella!</i>

59
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:54,380
I'm going to a convenience store, 
so you go on ahe—

60
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:56,440
Please use mine, if you'd like.

61
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:57,310
Huh?

62
00:05:58,490 --> 00:06:01,220
But then you'll get wet!

63
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:05,540
I always keep a collapsible 
umbrella in my bag.

64
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:12,740
<i>Not only did he bring an umbrella, 
but he keeps a spare on hand, too?</i>

65
00:06:22,130 --> 00:06:24,820
The wind's real strong...

66
00:06:25,410 --> 00:06:26,780
You doing okay?!

67
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:28,430
Yes, somehow...

68
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:35,540
Th-Thank y—

69
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:37,220
Use this umbrella instead!

70
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:39,660
What? No, I'm good!

71
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:41,580
You should use it, Senpai.

72
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:43,070
It's your umbrella!

73
00:06:43,070 --> 00:06:44,440
I'll borrow that one instead—

74
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:45,560
It's okay!

75
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:47,340
I can still use this one.

76
00:07:03,810 --> 00:07:08,460
If you show up drenched to the meeting, 
it'll only bother the others.

77
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:11,870
Oh! Y-You're right!

78
00:07:11,870 --> 00:07:13,570
I'll hold it, then.

79
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:17,470
Let's go!

80
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:18,710
Yeah.

81
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:24,940
<i>He's...</i>

82
00:07:24,940 --> 00:07:26,210
<i>so close!</i>

83
00:07:30,510 --> 00:07:32,720
Are you getting wet, Senpai?

84
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:34,370
I-I'm okay.

85
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:35,470
Keep your eyes forward.

86
00:07:35,470 --> 00:07:36,320
Yes, ma'am!

87
00:07:40,790 --> 00:07:43,620
<i>Was he always this tall?</i>

88
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:45,800
<i>Since he's closer, he feels even more...</i>

89
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:50,940
<i>This ain't the time to think like this!</i>

90
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:59,750
Thank you for coming 
despite the awful weather.

91
00:07:59,750 --> 00:08:03,000
No, thank you for having us.

92
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:08,660
We wanted you to see the
 finalized collab items directly.

93
00:08:10,020 --> 00:08:11,760
Thank you!

94
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:15,570
I'll have Kamegawa give you the details.

95
00:08:15,570 --> 00:08:17,150
Thank you for having me.

96
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:24,020
RACING GIRLS COLLAB CAFÉ

97
00:08:19,580 --> 00:08:24,300
Referencing the new tracks that are 
scheduled to release in the next update,

98
00:08:24,020 --> 00:08:28,650
5 TYPES OF PARFAITS

99
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:28,150
we're thinking of preparing 
five different parfaits.

100
00:08:28,650 --> 00:08:29,400
COLLAB GOODS

101
00:08:29,740 --> 00:08:34,290
These were designed in collaboration with the maid café we will be working with...

102
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:33,830
<i>This newbie's good at his job, as always.</i>

103
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:39,410
<i>In comparison, I forgot my umbrella 
and he had to lend me one...</i>

104
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:44,710
<i>I at least need to achieve my goal 
of sending him home early!</i>

105
00:08:53,530 --> 00:08:56,520
Even with our umbrellas, 
we can't avoid getting wet.

106
00:08:57,300 --> 00:08:58,350
Kamegawa.

107
00:08:58,350 --> 00:08:59,180
Yes?

108
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:03,350
Hold still.

109
00:09:04,710 --> 00:09:08,120
S-Sorry. Thank you.

110
00:09:20,790 --> 00:09:23,290
<i>This reminds me of my cat at my parent's place.</i>

111
00:09:25,210 --> 00:09:27,130
Take off your jacket and dry it.

112
00:09:27,130 --> 00:09:28,040
Okay.

113
00:09:29,460 --> 00:09:31,200
Are you okay with a latte?

114
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,030
Yeah.

115
00:09:32,030 --> 00:09:33,300
I'll go get that for you.

116
00:09:38,270 --> 00:09:41,430
<i>It'll get all wrinkly if he hangs it like that.</i>

117
00:09:45,770 --> 00:09:49,830
<i>How does one hang this kind of suit?</i>

118
00:09:51,470 --> 00:09:53,360
<i>Wow, it's huge.</i>

119
00:10:07,950 --> 00:10:10,070
Flap, flap, flap...

120
00:10:13,260 --> 00:10:14,460
Um...

121
00:10:22,210 --> 00:10:23,460
Thanks...

122
00:10:32,550 --> 00:10:35,820
Looks like it's going to hit Kanto 
sooner than expected.

123
00:10:39,130 --> 00:10:40,360
Something the matter?

124
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:41,050
Huh?

125
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:42,620
Ah, no.

126
00:10:44,770 --> 00:10:48,250
I was just thinking about 
how heavy the rain is.

127
00:10:49,230 --> 00:10:52,240
Are you perhaps... a bit excited about this?

128
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:53,260
Huh?

129
00:10:53,260 --> 00:10:55,300
Stare...

130
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:59,210
Sorry, I'm being imprudent, aren't I?

131
00:11:00,140 --> 00:11:02,680
It's just so unusual.

132
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:05,050
I can't help but feel a little restless.

133
00:11:05,810 --> 00:11:10,250
The longer you work, 
the less you'll say stuff like that.

134
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:12,630
You're still a child.

135
00:11:15,550 --> 00:11:19,080
B-But then what does that make you?

136
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:21,440
You were just playing with my suit.

137
00:11:22,970 --> 00:11:24,740
A-Are you all right?!

138
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:28,960
There are times I wanna 
be childish, too, y'know!

139
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:35,670
That one sounded really close.

140
00:11:36,340 --> 00:11:38,400
Calm down, calm down.

141
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:40,050
Y-You're right.

142
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:41,790
Sorry—

143
00:11:48,850 --> 00:11:51,050
This is a business district,

144
00:11:51,050 --> 00:11:53,150
so the lightning should 
hit a lightning rod...

145
00:11:53,640 --> 00:11:56,150
Y-You're right. Yeah.

146
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:05,320
Let's play shiritori!

147
00:12:07,390 --> 00:12:08,230
Ringo (apple).

148
00:12:09,060 --> 00:12:10,030
Gomi (trash).

149
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:12,560
Mikan (mandarin)... oops...

150
00:12:15,890 --> 00:12:19,200
You're the one who suggested the game...

151
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:22,920
The lightning's stopped now.

152
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:29,430
Okay. Let's get back to work.

153
00:12:29,430 --> 00:12:30,570
Yes, ma'am!

154
00:12:48,300 --> 00:12:50,970
You can head home first, Kamegawa.

155
00:12:50,970 --> 00:12:54,030
What? But I still have work...

156
00:12:54,030 --> 00:12:56,730
What you've gotten done is enough.

157
00:12:56,730 --> 00:12:59,790
Go home before the trains stop running.

158
00:13:00,410 --> 00:13:03,170
But you're going to stay, right?

159
00:13:03,170 --> 00:13:05,830
I'll have to work from home tomorrow, so...

160
00:13:06,270 --> 00:13:10,470
I need to finish what I can only do 
in the office now while I still can.

161
00:13:12,820 --> 00:13:15,980
Um, is there anything I can do to help?

162
00:13:16,870 --> 00:13:18,860
No, I'm all right.

163
00:13:19,420 --> 00:13:21,730
You can assign me anything, Senpai.

164
00:13:24,330 --> 00:13:25,110
Then...

165
00:13:25,870 --> 00:13:31,130
Sorry to ask, but could you go get the 
documents from Sales before they leave?

166
00:13:31,130 --> 00:13:32,200
Roger.

167
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:35,710
I'm going to attend an online meeting now.

168
00:13:36,230 --> 00:13:38,900
Just leave the documents on my desk.

169
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:40,930
You can go home after that.

170
00:13:40,930 --> 00:13:41,790
Yes, ma'am.

171
00:13:48,550 --> 00:13:51,380
How is he such a kind creature?

172
00:13:53,820 --> 00:13:57,190
Excuse me, can I have a moment?

173
00:13:57,190 --> 00:13:58,790
Coming.

174
00:13:59,190 --> 00:14:00,690
Huh? Kamegawa?!

175
00:14:00,690 --> 00:14:02,330
Tsukahara-senpai!

176
00:14:02,330 --> 00:14:03,690
It's been a while!

177
00:14:03,730 --> 00:14:07,200
SALES DEPARTMENT - SHUN TSUKAHARA

178
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:07,640
What're you doing, coming in on a day like this?

179
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:10,320
They're working the rookie to the bone!

180
00:14:11,010 --> 00:14:12,770
Not at all.

181
00:14:12,770 --> 00:14:15,960
What about you, Senpai? 
You're not working from home today?

182
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:19,670
Yeah, the payment deadline is crazy today.

183
00:14:21,590 --> 00:14:25,010
I could really use a helping hand right now.

184
00:14:30,890 --> 00:14:33,530
That concludes today's meeting.

185
00:14:33,530 --> 00:14:35,050
Thank you for your time.

186
00:14:35,050 --> 00:14:36,480
<i>Thank you.</i>

187
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:37,310
<i>Excuse us.</i>

188
00:14:37,310 --> 00:14:38,450
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

189
00:14:38,450 --> 00:14:39,260
<i>Good work today.</i>

190
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:41,150
<i>Thank you for your continued support.</i>

191
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:47,400
YOU HAVE LEFT THE MEETING

192
00:14:43,230 --> 00:14:45,820
I managed to finish my work.

193
00:14:47,710 --> 00:14:50,660
Are the trains even runnin' now?

194
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:55,870
I'm glad I was at least able to 
send Kamegawa home early.

195
00:14:57,870 --> 00:14:59,120
Good work today!

196
00:14:59,120 --> 00:14:59,950
You're—

197
00:15:00,290 --> 00:15:02,680
What are you doing?! Why are you here?!

198
00:15:02,680 --> 00:15:04,760
What if the last train's already left?!

199
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:06,660
I thought I said you could head home...

200
00:15:06,660 --> 00:15:08,210
No, I definitely said that!

201
00:15:08,210 --> 00:15:09,550
I'm sorry, I—

202
00:15:09,550 --> 00:15:12,100
Hurry and pack up. We're going home.

203
00:15:12,910 --> 00:15:15,260
I'm going to stay a bit longer.

204
00:15:16,330 --> 00:15:17,220
What's that?!

205
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:20,000
I was asked to help out a bit.

206
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,070
Asked? By who?

207
00:15:22,520 --> 00:15:24,830
Tsukahara-san from Sales.

208
00:15:24,830 --> 00:15:27,480
He helped me out back 
when I was job searching.

209
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:33,410
He said he could use my help 
if I happened to be free, so...

210
00:15:35,010 --> 00:15:36,010
Senpai?

211
00:15:43,190 --> 00:15:44,080
Hey!

212
00:15:46,420 --> 00:15:47,500
Kannawa...

213
00:15:47,910 --> 00:15:49,690
And Kamegawa?

214
00:15:49,690 --> 00:15:51,840
What brings you two here?

215
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:54,590
I'm Kamegawa's mentor.

216
00:15:55,220 --> 00:15:57,530
Oh, I see.

217
00:15:57,530 --> 00:15:58,630
And?

218
00:15:58,630 --> 00:16:01,740
Was there something wrong 
with the documents I just gave you?

219
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:06,610
Could you please refrain from pushing 
work onto someone else's subordinate?

220
00:16:06,610 --> 00:16:07,610
Huh?

221
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:13,480
Wait, I only asked if he happened 
to be free... Right?

222
00:16:15,130 --> 00:16:17,450
If you can't do it, that's fine.

223
00:16:17,740 --> 00:16:19,580
I didn't force it on him or anything.

224
00:16:19,580 --> 00:16:22,960
Being "asked" by a senior 
is the same as "forcing."

225
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:28,460
You know that, and that's
 why you asked him.

226
00:16:28,460 --> 00:16:32,840
Kamegawa's saying that he's going to 
work overtime because of <i>your</i> work.

227
00:16:38,100 --> 00:16:40,850
Do your own job.

228
00:16:40,850 --> 00:16:44,680
I won't tolerate my precious junior
 working overtime on a day like this!

229
00:16:51,780 --> 00:16:52,990
My bad.

230
00:16:53,260 --> 00:16:55,210
Oh, no worries!

231
00:16:55,210 --> 00:16:56,490
Excuse me.

232
00:16:58,260 --> 00:16:59,120
Um...

233
00:16:59,650 --> 00:17:01,100
Thank you.

234
00:17:01,950 --> 00:17:04,120
Just tell him "no" next time.

235
00:17:04,730 --> 00:17:05,580
Yes, ma'am.

236
00:17:12,450 --> 00:17:14,910
Are the trains still running?

237
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:21,530
Looks like just barely, yes.

238
00:17:22,060 --> 00:17:24,600
Th-Then let's head to the station.

239
00:17:42,120 --> 00:17:43,900
I-It's okay.

240
00:17:43,900 --> 00:17:47,040
In weather like this, it makes no difference 
whether you have an umbrella or not.

241
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:49,050
Senpai!

242
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:52,550
Would you like to share an umbrella 
until we reach the station?

243
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:59,460
N-No... The station's right there, 
so we can just run—

244
00:17:59,460 --> 00:18:00,930
It's not safe!

245
00:18:00,930 --> 00:18:03,720
The wind's pretty strong. 
If something were to hit you...

246
00:18:05,150 --> 00:18:08,650
I may not be that useful on the job yet,

247
00:18:08,970 --> 00:18:11,830
but I believe I can be of use 
in times like these.

248
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:14,650
I may be your junior, but I'm also a man.

249
00:18:16,530 --> 00:18:20,080
Wait, that came out weird.

250
00:18:20,080 --> 00:18:21,680
I meant I have a man's strength!

251
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:22,640
Strength!

252
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:24,540
R-Right.

253
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:30,840
Shall we go?

254
00:18:31,210 --> 00:18:32,100
Uh-huh.

255
00:18:39,470 --> 00:18:41,120
Are you okay?

256
00:18:46,150 --> 00:18:48,740
<i>A junior, but also a man...</i>

257
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:51,180
<i>I knew that, but...</i>

258
00:19:14,270 --> 00:19:18,420
You were right, Senpai. 
I don't think the umbrella's helping.

259
00:19:18,730 --> 00:19:21,050
No, it's helping!

260
00:19:22,790 --> 00:19:24,350
Back then...

261
00:19:24,350 --> 00:19:26,980
I was just panicking.

262
00:19:28,690 --> 00:19:31,220
S-Sorry, I just...

263
00:19:31,220 --> 00:19:32,200
It's okay.

264
00:19:34,150 --> 00:19:35,020
Hey!

265
00:19:35,020 --> 00:19:38,530
You don't need to lean that 
toward me so much. You'll get wet.

266
00:19:38,530 --> 00:19:40,220
But...

267
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:45,280
Then could you please lean more toward me?

268
00:19:45,660 --> 00:19:46,510
Huh?

269
00:19:55,350 --> 00:19:57,960
I-Isn't it hard to walk?

270
00:19:58,460 --> 00:19:59,830
I'm okay!

271
00:20:13,570 --> 00:20:16,540
<i>Thank you for using the train system.</i>

272
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:17,780
I didn't know we took the same train.

273
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:20,560
<i>We will soon arrive at Akabane. Akabane.</i>

274
00:20:17,780 --> 00:20:18,750
Me neither.

275
00:20:19,100 --> 00:20:23,680
You always stayed longer at 
the office, so I had no idea.

276
00:20:21,050 --> 00:20:24,970
<i>Please make sure you have 
all of your belongings.</i>

277
00:20:25,390 --> 00:20:27,780
<i>The doors on the right side will open.</i>

278
00:20:27,690 --> 00:20:29,930
We sure got wet.

279
00:20:28,290 --> 00:20:32,160
<i>The next station is Akabane, JA15.</i>

280
00:20:29,930 --> 00:20:33,320
It was raining buckets, after all.

281
00:20:32,160 --> 00:20:34,500
<i>The doors on the right side will open.</i>

282
00:20:34,820 --> 00:20:39,340
<i>Please change here for the Keihin-Tohoku Line, the Utsunomiya Line,</i>

283
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:40,160
Thanks for your help today. With everything.

284
00:20:39,340 --> 00:20:42,640
<i>the Takasaki Line, and the Ueno-Tokyo Line.</i>

285
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:43,760
No way. I should be the one thanking you.

286
00:20:47,250 --> 00:20:49,450
Oh. This is my stop.

287
00:20:49,450 --> 00:20:50,460
Senpai!

288
00:20:51,770 --> 00:20:53,940
Please take this, if you'd like.

289
00:20:54,270 --> 00:20:55,020
Huh?

290
00:20:56,340 --> 00:20:58,420
I live close to the station, so...

291
00:20:58,420 --> 00:21:00,250
It's okay if it breaks, too.

292
00:21:03,970 --> 00:21:05,570
Th-Then... here.

293
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:07,820
It's better than nothing.

294
00:21:08,690 --> 00:21:10,100
Thank you.

295
00:21:10,890 --> 00:21:13,720
<i>The train on track 8 is now departing.</i>

296
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:15,460
I'll see you tomorrow, then.

297
00:21:14,310 --> 00:21:16,750
<i>Please stand clear of the closing doors.</i>

298
00:21:15,460 --> 00:21:17,390
Oh, wait, it'll be remote.

299
00:21:17,390 --> 00:21:18,820
Good work, anyway!

300
00:21:21,550 --> 00:21:22,800
Good work today!

301
00:21:41,130 --> 00:21:44,300
I'm so glad we work from home tomorrow.

302
00:21:49,570 --> 00:21:53,450
I wouldn't know how to face him...

303
00:22:04,570 --> 00:22:09,590
Should I buy some 
nice-smelling fabric softener?

